<HR size="1" color="#5d7790">
<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
Which way do we want to go here?<P><B>1) Kill Gaints to gain Dorf and Dragon?</B>  <I>Long range plans like hunting in Western Wastes and easier ports in WL/CS make this a good choice. Gain two Armor quests. Also gain two SoV cities to base from.</I><BR><B>2) Kill Dragons and Dorfs to gain Giant?</B><I>Short range, this gives us some rather nice equipment and gives us a huge range of things to kill.  Long range, the Giant quest armor is awesome for melee classes with super high AC's.  Makes ports a tad harder...but not that much harder. Only one city to use as a base.</I><BR><B>3) Kill Giants and Dragons because we can?</B><I>Gives us good dorf faction for the Thurgadin Armor quests and nice gear to wear while we wait for the levels to come. Puts just about everything on the menu for exp. Only one city to use as a base.</I><P>The main reasons I bring this up are, 1) Erlas worships Rallos Zek...he's currently NOT KOS to the giants.  2) Some real nice armor drops in Skyshrine ( Dragon ) and some other real nice armor drops off the dorfs in Thurgadin.  +36 AC BP in Icewall keep make anyone else drool?<P>If we go with 2 or 3, then main downside is ports into Wakening Lands and Cobalt Scar.  Wakening Lands is totally out due to Woushi there and seeing thru inviso. Cobalt Scar isn't that big of a deal..inviso works here.  Faction also takes a ton of work...so it would be awhile before we had a bank/vendor that we could use in Velious once we started destroying Dorfs.<P>If we decide to go with #1, then I think plans for hunting in SkyShrine should be put off and we just move to Kael.  Nothing real nice drops from the giants there...but it's good dorf and dragon faction while getting exp.  Once the Alpha group hits 50'ish...we might be able to move deeper into Kael and start getting Thurg or SkyShrine quest armor drops.  Also makes hunting in CS easier without needing to worry about the Drakes or Wyverns as much.<P>--------------------<P>Verser - Bard of the 51st Song
</FONT>
