</FONT>
<HR size="1" color="#5d7790">
<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
Well, I'll throw in my opinions on this, pros and cons for all 3 options as I see it.<P>1.  Kill Gaints to gain Dorf and Dragon<BR>Pros<BR>Two cities to use<BR>No worries about woushi.<BR>A few decent things drop in Kael.  <BR>Cons<BR>If you ever get to the point of being able to kill dragons, you won't be able to.  <BR>Only 1 wing of ToV is open to dragon allied folks, and guess what... its already crowded with all the other dragon allied guilds.  Much squabbling to come.<BR>Miss out on all the Velium Etched armor in Icewell Keep.<BR>Miss out on all the Guardian/Sentry armor in Skyshrine.<BR>Dragon Faction quests are DAMN hard, don't expect many of us to be doing them anytime soon, if ever.<P>2. Kill Dragons and Dorfs to gain Giant<BR>Pros<BR>Access to velium Etched Armor in Icewell Keep.<BR>Access to Guardian/Sentry armor in Skyshrine.<BR>Best AC quested armor.<BR>Better options for exp as you get higher up in levels.<BR>You get to kill dwarves (who needs any other reason? :P)<BR>Can Hunt all of ToV.<BR>Cons<BR>Only 1 city for banking/vending.<BR>Ports into CS and WL can be ugly.<BR>Armor Quests aren't particularly easy.<BR>Don't get the opportunity to do the coldain shawl or coldain ring quests.<P>3. Kill Giants and Dragons because we can<BR>Pros<BR>Easiest Route to take as you already have decent faction with dwarves.<BR>Lots of stuff to kill for exp.<BR>Access to Guardian/Sentry armor.<BR>Access to worst, but easiest, quested armor.<BR>Can hunt all of ToV.<BR>Get the opportunity to do the coldain shawl/ring quests.<BR>Cons<BR>Only one city for banking/vending<BR>ports into CS and WL can ugly<BR>Getting thru Kael can be ugly<P>I think if Division Thirteen has no plans to grow beyond its current status, then option 3 is probably the best one.  As it stands D13 won't be doing ToV, Western Wastes, Dragon Quests, etc. for a VERY long time, if ever.  I have no idea how large, or competent, the guilds with which we are aligned are.  Raiding PoG, PoH, PoF, and such are all admirable achievements, but pale in comparison to yelinak, ToV, WW.  In considering which faction to take, you have to decide why you want that faction?  Ease of use? Roleplaying?  Uber loot?  Myself?  I don't think we'll ever really "need" dragon faction so I'm currently at ally faction with kromzek, and KOS to kromrif (still working on this one).  I don't plan to ruin the faction work I've put in so far, but if we come to a decision on which faction(s) we are going to go with, I'll work on changing it if needed.
</FONT>
